# Repo-root .dockerignore. Both deploy/php/Dockerfile and deploy/nginx's Dockerfile
# (Task 3) build with the REPO ROOT as context and COPY backend/ / frontend/
# wholesale. Docker does NOT consult .gitignore, so without this file every
# gitignored local artifact on the build host -- most importantly real secrets in
# backend/.env / frontend/.env -- gets copied into a public GHCR image, where
# `docker history` and the filesystem are readable by anyone. This file is the
# only thing standing between a normal dev checkout and a leaked SMTP/DB/app-key
# credential (see task-2-report.md, Critical finding).

# Real per-environment secrets. .env.example files are tracked templates, not
# secrets, but nothing in either image needs them either, so the wildcard is fine.
backend/.env*
frontend/.env*

# Dependency trees: both Dockerfiles install these fresh inside the build (composer
# install / npm ci), so the host's copy is never needed and would otherwise
# overwrite the image's own --no-dev / production install (see task-2-report.md).
backend/vendor
backend/node_modules
frontend/node_modules

# Local-only artifacts a fresh CI checkout never has, but a dev host does.
backend/public/storage
backend/storage/*.key
backend/storage/pail
backend/auth.json
backend/database/*.sqlite
frontend/dist
frontend/test-results
frontend/playwright-report

# General context bloat, never needed inside either image.
.git
.superpowers
node_modules
temp
test-results
